{
  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best configuration (config_019, acc 0.639) uses pca_n2000 as the RNA encoder with weighted fusion, avgpool aggregation, resnet50 image encoder, and multiprofile. All completed experiments have used only pca_n2000, leaving the RNA encoder choice (scvi_n200 vs scgpt vs PCA) as the largest unexplored design dimension. config_031 tests scvi_n200 while holding all other parameters at their known-best settings (multimodal, multiprofile, resnet50, avgpool, weighted). This directly clarifies whether a learned nonlinear encoder captures complementary biological structure that PCA misses, which would be especially relevant in the multimodal setting where the RNA branch must provide a strong, informative representation to fuse with the image branch. If scvi_n200 matches or exceeds PCA, it opens a productive new axis; if it underperforms, it confirms PCA's sufficiency and redirects budget toward other dimensions (e.g., transformer aggregation or image encoder refinement). This is the highest-information single experiment under the limited budget because it isolates one major design variable against the current best baseline."
}

